\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Change in paired accuracy across fixed intervention magnitudes $|\alpha |=1$--$5$ for the causal direction and ten norm-matched random directions; points show mean changes and error bars show 95\% bootstrap CIs. Negative values indicate reduced discrimination between critical and control contexts. The causal-direction CI bootstraps the 150 item pairs; the random-direction CI jointly bootstraps directions and the shared item pairs. \textbf  {In five models, increasing the causal intervention increasingly reduces paired accuracy and generally has a larger effect than the random baseline; Qwen3 4B shows no reliable effect, while Llama~3.1 70B changes in the opposite direction.}}}{5}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:intervention-alpha-sweep}{{4}{5}{Change in paired accuracy across fixed intervention magnitudes $|\alpha |=1$--$5$ for the causal direction and ten norm-matched random directions; points show mean changes and error bars show 95\% bootstrap CIs. Negative values indicate reduced discrimination between critical and control contexts. The causal-direction CI bootstraps the 150 item pairs; the random-direction CI jointly bootstraps directions and the shared item pairs. \textbf {In five models, increasing the causal intervention increasingly reduces paired accuracy and generally has a larger effect than the random baseline; Qwen3 4B shows no reliable effect, while Llama~3.1 70B changes in the opposite direction.}}{figure.caption.10}{}}
